35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Oh no! I saw the bin house, and it's a disaster! It smells way worse in the summer because you can't hose it out. We definitely shouldn't do that, or it'll be super stinky!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It's a relief we checked that, Rin. Regarding the money, we're spending quite a bit on maintenance already, and a new shelter is expensive even with the subsidy. We must be very careful not to overspend.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,It seems we have a classic case of one person bearing the brunt of the frustration. The complaint log is practically a diary of one household's misery. We can't just ignore that emotional baggage.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"It's not just about the money or the smell. I found that ""simple"" supervision takes nearly an hour each time, and the station block is already fighting over who sweeps. We can't let this become another chore for one person.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical data is concerning. One frontage is far too narrow, and another is obstructed by a driveway. Furthermore, the ward's filing process is tedious; frequent site changes would be a bureaucratic nightmare for us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But if we don't do something, it'll stay smelly! If the bin house is a bad idea and supervision takes too long, maybe there's a way to keep it open but make it cleaner?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree, but we have to be realistic. We're already spending over thirty thousand yen annually on basics. If we add a costly new system, it might be too much for some of our neighbors to afford.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be honest: the money is a secondary issue. The real problem is that one neighbor is reaching their breaking point. If we don't solve the resentment, no amount of money will fix the atmosphere.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. Resentment grows when the workload is invisible. If we just ""agree"" to a plan without a strict schedule, the most helpful person will end up doing everything. We need a system that doesn't rely on kindness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"If we cannot easily rotate the site due to the narrow frontages and the ward's strict filing requirements, we must address the current imbalance. It is unfair for one household to permanently host the point.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want anyone to be sad or grumpy! If we can't move the bins and we can't build a smelly house, maybe we can just find a way to make cleaning it super fast and fun?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Making it fun is a lovely thought, Rin, but we must consider the cost. If we buy expensive equipment to make cleaning easier, we're adding to a budget that's already strained. We need a low-cost, sustainable solution.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"""Fun"" isn't going to fix a three-year grudge, Rin. We have a neighbor who feels besieged by trash and a group of people too polite to actually enforce rules. We need a solution that restores peace, not a party.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Peace is great, but peace usually comes at the cost of someone's free time. If we just ""agree"" to be better, the same person will end up sweeping. We need a plan with a hard time-limit.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We must stop focusing on ""feelings"" and look at the facts. Since rotation is physically and legally impractical, we cannot simply move the bins. We must find a way to compensate the hosting household fairly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"Compensate them? Like with treats or helping them clean? If we can't move the bins, we have to make sure the person living next to them doesn't have to smell the stinky stuff alone!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"Helping with cleaning is a wonderful idea, but we should be careful about financial compensation too. If we pay the hosting household, we must ensure the amount is fair and affordable for everyone involved.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Treats and payments are just bandages. The real issue is that nobody wants to be the ""bad guy"" who rejects a late bag. If we don't solve that social tension, we're just paying for the privilege of staying angry.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"Exactly. We can't just pay people to be miserable. If we don't define exactly how many minutes of work this is and who does it when, we're just setting ourselves up for another burnout. Let's be precise.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Precision is exactly what we need. We have a physical reality where only a few spots are viable and a legal reality that makes moving the point difficult. We must now quantify the burden of the current host.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
