60,3,1,talk,Rin,,I'm voting against Option C! I saw that bin house and it was super stinky in the summer. We can't build a smelly box that we can't even wash!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin. Option C is far too expensive, and the maintenance costs would be a heavy burden on our budgets. I think we should look for a more affordable alternative.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option B is a fantasy given the physical constraints Asuka found. Forcing a rotation into narrow driveways will just create new grudges. We need a solution that acknowledges the current host's pain without causing a neighborhood war.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A is the only one that actually addresses the labor. If we set a strict window and a clear rotation, we can track the hours and ensure no one is stuck doing all the work.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is physically impossible for some households and legally impractical due to the ward's filing requirements. Option C ignores the maintenance issues. Option A is the only logical choice, provided the host's burden is acknowledged.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we do Option A, can we make sure the person overseeing it helps clean up the smells? I don't want the corner to be yucky for the person living there!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"That's a kind thought, Rin. As long as we don't buy expensive equipment, I'm okay with that. Option A is the most budget-friendly choice and won't put an unfair financial strain on any of us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"The key is that Option A forces us to actually talk to each other and coordinate. If we can manage a schedule without fighting, we might actually start acting like neighbors again. It's the most human choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"As long as the schedule is written in stone and not just a ""suggestion,"" I'm in. Let's make sure the time commitment is explicit so nobody ends up as the default manager.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Option A is the only viable path. However, we must explicitly acknowledge that the host still bears the spatial burden. The rotation of oversight must be strictly enforced to ensure labor is shared equally.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm happy with Option A! It's not a smelly box, and if we all take turns, the person living there won't feel so alone with the stinky trash. Let's make it a clean corner!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm also happy with Option A. It's the most sustainable choice for our wallets and ensures that no one is burdened by a sudden, large expense. Let's go with the most affordable and fair plan.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm in for Option A. It's the only one that doesn't ignore the physical reality or the social tension. If we can handle a schedule, we might actually survive as neighbors.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm voting for Option A. It's the only way to quantify the labor and stop the cycle of burnout. Let's just keep the rules strict so the ""kindest"" person doesn't end up doing everything.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I concur. Option A is the only choice that respects the physical constraints of our frontages and the ward's regulations while distributing the labor. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone agrees! Let's make our corner super clean and happy so nobody has to be grumpy about the trash anymore. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I vote for Option A. It's the most considerate choice for everyone's budget, and I'm glad we found a way to be fair without causing financial stress. Let's work together to keep it sustainable!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for Option A. It's the only way to stop the bleeding and actually address the resentment. Let's hope we can follow a schedule without starting a new war.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for Option A. Let's just make sure that schedule is ironclad so we don't end up with one person doing all the heavy lifting. I'm looking forward to a fair system!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option A. It is the only solution that aligns with the physical and legal constraints while ensuring the labor is shared. We must now formalize the schedule to maintain this equity.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
